title: 'pallet-collective: include the voting threshold in the proposal hash'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    A proposal in `pallet_collective` is now identified by the hash of the SCALE encoding of
    `(call, threshold)` instead of the hash of the call alone. The same call proposed with
    different thresholds therefore results in distinct proposals. The derivation is exposed as
    `Pallet::<T, I>::proposal_hash(&call, threshold)`.

    The pallet's storage version is bumped to 5. Runtimes must add
    `pallet_collective::migrations::v5::MigrateToV5<Runtime, Instance>` to their migrations for
    every instance of the pallet. The migration re-keys all active proposals in `Proposals`,
    `ProposalOf`, `Voting` and `CostOf` under the new hash; it is bounded by `MaxProposals` and
    runs in a single block.

    Breaking changes:
    - `Pallet::do_propose_execute` takes the `threshold` as its first argument.
    - Off-chain tooling that computed the proposal hash as `hash(call)` to call `vote`, `close`
      or `disapprove_proposal` must now compute `hash((call, threshold))`, or read the hash from
      the `Proposed` event.
- audience: Runtime User
  description: |-
    The Alliance collective on Collectives Westend runs a one-off storage migration that re-keys
    its active motions. Motion hashes shown by tooling change accordingly.
crates:
- name: pallet-collective
  bump: major
- name: pallet-alliance
  bump: none
- name: pallet-utility
  bump: none
- name: collectives-westend-runtime
  bump: patch
- name: kitchensink-runtime
  bump: patch
